## 5. Data Model

### 5.1 Sub-Agent Instance Identifier

**Format:** `sub_{agent_type}_{global_counter}`

**Examples:**
```
sub_web_research_001
sub_financial_analyst_042
sub_code_reviewer_123
sub_test_writer_001  ← Can be child of sub_code_reviewer_123
```

**Components:**
- `agent_type`: Short name (e.g., `web_research`, `financial_analyst`)
- `global_counter`: Sequential counter across all sub-agents (zero-padded)

**Rationale:**
- **Shorter IDs**: Avoids exponential growth with nesting depth
- **File-system safe**: No special characters, stays under path limits
- **Parent-agnostic**: Parent relationship stored in metadata, not ID
- **Human-readable**: Clear purpose from agent_type
- **Unique**: Global counter ensures no collisions

**Parent Relationship:**
- Stored in session metadata under `parent_session.session_id`
- Allows full chain navigation: sub → parent → grandparent → root
- No ID length explosion at deep nesting levels

### 5.2 Session File Structure

#### 5.2.1 Coordinator Session (Root or Sub-Agent)

```json
{
  "session_id": "abc123",
  "user_id": "admin",
  "created_at": "2025-10-30T10:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2025-10-30T10:15:00Z",
  "title": "AI Regulation Research",
  "agent_name": "meta_agent",
  "llm_profile": "default",
  "depth": 1,
  
  "messages": [
    {"role": "user", "content": "Research latest AI regulations"},
    {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll use web_research_agent...", 
     "tool_calls": [...]},
    {"role": "tool", "name": "web_research_agent", 
     "content": "{...result from sub-agent...}"}
  ],
  
  "metadata": {
    "message_count": 3,
    "sub_agents": {
      "sub_web_research_001": {
        "instance_id": "sub_web_research_001",
        "agent_type": "web_research_agent",
        "created_at": "2025-10-30T10:01:00Z",
        "last_used": "2025-10-30T10:05:00Z",
        "status": "active",
        "task_summary": "Research latest AI regulations",
        "message_count": 12,
        "depth": 2
      }
    }
  }
}
```

#### 5.2.2 Sub-Agent Session (Can Also Be Coordinator)

```json
{
  "session_id": "sub_web_research_001",
  "user_id": "admin",
  "created_at": "2025-10-30T10:01:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2025-10-30T10:05:00Z",
  "title": "Research latest AI regulations (sub-agent)",
  "agent_name": "web_research_agent",
  "llm_profile": "chat",
  "depth": 2,
  
  "parent_session": {
    "session_id": "abc123",
    "agent_name": "meta_agent",
    "created_at": "2025-10-30T10:01:00Z"
  },
  
  "messages": [
    {"role": "user", "content": "Research latest AI regulations"},
    {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll search for...", 
     "tool_calls": [{"name": "duckduckgo_search", ...}]},
    {"role": "tool", "name": "duckduckgo_search", 
     "content": "[...search results...]"},
    {"role": "assistant", "content": "Found 5 key regulations..."}
  ],
  
  "tool_state": {
    "sequential_thinking": {
      "session_id": "st_sub_web_research_001",
      "thoughts_count": 15,
      "current_branch": "main",
      "last_thought": "Need to analyze GDPR implications..."
    }
  },
  
  "metadata": {
    "message_count": 12,
    "sub_agents": {
      "sub_scholar_042": {
        "instance_id": "sub_scholar_042",
        "agent_type": "scholar_agent",
        "created_at": "2025-10-30T10:03:00Z",
        "status": "active",
        "depth": 3
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**Key Properties:**
- `depth`: Nesting level (1=root session, 2=sub-agent, 3=sub-sub-agent, etc.)
- `parent_session`: Link to parent (null for root sessions)
- `metadata.sub_agents`: Map of child sub-agents (if any)

### 5.3 Schema Extensions

**New Fields in All Sessions:**

```python
class SessionSchema:
    depth: int  # NEW - Nesting level (1=root, 2=sub, 3=sub-sub, etc.)
    metadata: SessionMetadata  # Extended
    
class SessionMetadata:
    sub_agents: Dict[str, SubAgentMetadata]  # NEW - Map of child sub-agents
    
class SubAgentMetadata:
    instance_id: str
    agent_type: str
    created_at: datetime
    last_used: datetime
    status: str  # active | completed | archived | failed
    task_summary: str
    message_count: int
    depth: int  # NEW - Child's nesting level
```

**New Fields in Sub-Agent Sessions Only:**

```python
class SubAgentSession:
    parent_session: ParentSessionInfo  # NEW - Link to parent
    tool_state: Dict[str, Any]  # NEW - Persistent tool state
    
class ParentSessionInfo:
    session_id: str
    agent_name: str
    created_at: datetime
```

**Depth Tracking:**
- Root session: `depth = 1`
- Sub-agent: `depth = parent.depth + 1`
- Max depth check: `if depth > max_nesting_depth: raise Error`

