## Appendix A: Example Workflows

### A.1 Research Assistant Workflow

```python
# User starts conversation with meta_agent
user_message = "I need to research the latest developments in quantum computing"

# meta_agent decides to use web_research_agent
coordinator_response = await meta_agent.run(user_message)

# Tool call: create_sub_agent
{
  "tool": "create_sub_agent",
  "arguments": {
    "agent_type": "web_research_agent",
    "task": "Research latest developments in quantum computing"
  }
}

# Response: Sub-agent created
{
  "instance_id": "abc123_sub_web_research_001",
  "status": "created"
}

# Sub-agent performs research, uses sequential_thinking
# Returns summary to coordinator

# Later: User asks follow-up
user_message = "Based on that research, which companies are leading?"

# Coordinator sees active sub-agent in system prompt
# Tool call: continue_sub_agent
{
  "tool": "continue_sub_agent",
  "arguments": {
    "instance_id": "abc123_sub_web_research_001",
    "message": "Which companies are leading in quantum computing?"
  }
}

# Sub-agent continues with full context from previous research
# Returns targeted answer about leading companies
```

### A.2 Code Review Workflow

```python
# User: "Review this Python file for security issues"
# Coordinator creates code_reviewer_agent sub-agent

# Sub-agent uses script_interpreter, finds issues
# Returns initial findings

# User: "Can you fix those issues and run tests?"
# Coordinator continues same sub-agent instance
# Sub-agent has context of previous findings
# Generates fixes, runs tests, returns results

# User: "Looks good, clean up"
# Coordinator deletes sub-agent
{
  "tool": "delete_sub_agent",
  "arguments": {
    "instance_id": "abc123_sub_code_reviewer_001"
  }
}
```

